 ## Overview
-Face-based volume rendering with edge highlights renders volumetric data by treating individual cells (faces) as the primary sampling unit, applying a scalar-based colormap for the body, and superimposing anti-aliased edge highlights to enhance structural clarity [S1, unofficial]. It differs from silhouette-based methods by detecting edges locally within each cell based on vertex attribute discontinuities or importance factors, rather than relying on global view-dependent depth discontinuities [S1, unofficial]. This approach provides consistent edge visibility regardless of camera orientation, making it suitable for interactive exploration where structural boundaries must remain distinct from the volume interior [S1, unofficial].
